nd Hornbill perched on a termite mound.\n- **Frames 14–24**: Immediate transition to Hadeda Ibis wading and drinking in a muddy puddle.\n- **Frames 25–30**: Wide shot of savannah with a small antelope grazing in the distance — no zebras, no wading birds.\n\n---\n\n✅ Final Answers:\n\n1. The bird appears on the rock from **Frame 1 to Frame 13**.\n2. Immediately after (starting Frame 14), a **wading bird (Hadeda Ibis) is shown drinking water**.\n3. **No zebras appear** in any of the 30 frames.\n4. **Yes, a wading bird (Hadeda Ibis) is drinking water** from Frame 14 to Frame 24.\n\nThe transition from the hornbill on the mound to the ibis at the waterhole is abrupt but clearly sequential, marking a shift in both subject and habitat within the documentary’s observational style.'}, {'batch_start': 30, 'batch_end': 40, 'image_paths': ['/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2720.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2721.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2722.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2723.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2724.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2725.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2726.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2727.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2728.jpg', '/mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/GcRKREorGSc/frames/frame_2729.jpg'], 'response': 'Based on the sequence of the 10 provided frames, here is the analysis addressing your specific questions:\n\n---\n\n**1) When does the bird appear on the rock?**\n\n- **The bird does not appear on a rock in any of these 10 frames.**\n- In Frames 1–5, there is a small, dark animal (possibly a bird or small mammal) visible in the middle distance on the grassy plain, but it is not perc